OL,3,GNEWSAPersistent fly-tipper fined for
OL,4,Ayear-long spree
OL,5,
OL,6,FA persistent fly-tipper has pleaded
OL,7,Fguilty to dumping rubbish on six
OL,8,Fseparate occasions across a town over
OL,9,Fthe course of a year.
OL,11,FMaria Irina Notar, 25, from Countess
OL,12,FRoad, Northampton, was ordered to pay
OL,13,Fcosts and fines totalling more than
OL,14,F#3,200 by Wellingborough Magistrates'
OL,15,FCourt.
OL,17,FWest Northamptonshire Council, who
OL,18,Fbrought the prosecution, said that
OL,19,Fbetween July 2024 and July 2025 Notar
OL,20,Fhad left piles of rubbish on East
OL,21,FStreet, Northampton, the area where she
OL,22,Fhad previously lived.
OL,23,APub: 08-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,368,360,200,160,0,100
